        ("The Development Monitoring and Evaluation Office and its mandate", "The Development Monitoring and Evaluation Office is an attached office of NITI Aayog whose own website, read on 2 September 2026, states that it was constituted in September 2015 by merging the erstwhile Program Evaluation Office and the Independent Evaluation Office, that it is mandated to actively monitor and evaluate the implementation of schemes, programmes and initiatives of the Government of India in order to strengthen their implementation and scope of delivery on an ongoing basis, and that this requires tracking performance, determining outcomes, diagnosing reasons for poor performance and generating recommendations for course correction; it is an evaluator without authority to redesign, so its findings must be adopted by the line ministry to have effect."),
